--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -11,3 +11,8 @@ Each task has a stable, list-unique string `id`. The ID is assigned when `add` s
 the same when the task is renamed. Use `get(id)` to retrieve a task by ID. `find`, `complete`,
 `reopen`, `rename`, `tag`, `untag` and `remove` accept either a task title or its ID; IDs take
 precedence if a string matches both.
+
+Tasks include ISO-8601 `createdAt` and `updatedAt` timestamps. `createdAt` is set when a task is
+added and remains unchanged; `updatedAt` is set at creation and refreshed by each successful task
+change. `createTodoList` accepts an optional function returning the current timestamp, which is useful
+when the caller needs to provide a clock; by default it uses the current time.
